{
    "test_name": "MOB.800_Search_StructuredQuery",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.800_Search_StructuredQuery",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.800` Build a structured filter on Asset Lookup and prove it filters.\n- READ-ONLY. Filters are client state feeding query variables; nothing is written.\n- This is the **advanced** filter system, distinct from the simple search/sort in\n  MOB.530. It builds SERVER-SIDE query conditions, so a defect returns wrong data\n  rather than a visibly broken control.\n- Proves filtering with a matched pair: `name contains Pump 0102` must SHOW the asset,\n  and `name contains ZZZZ-NO-SUCH-ASSET` must HIDE it. The negative leg is the one that proves\n  the filter is actually applied rather than merely accepted.\n- Each leg runs with EXACTLY ONE filter active \u2014 the test clears between them. Adding a\n  second contradictory filter did not hide the asset, so multi-filter combination is\n  not AND as assumed; that is an open question, not something to build on.\n- The positive leg asserts on a RESULT ROW, not page text: the active-filter pill\n  echoes the value you filtered on, so page-contains would pass against zero results.\n- The drawer does not close itself after 'Add Filter' (`addFilter` only calls\n  `onChange`), so the test closes it. No re-search is needed: `filters` feeds the\n  useQuery variables and Apollo re-runs on change.",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Search",
            "read-only",
            "StructuredQuery"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
        "config": {
            "assertions": [],
            "config_variables": [
